On Jul 7, 12:57 pm, Topi Linkala <n...@iki.fi> wrote:
> Hello to all but those that have killfiled me.
>
> As there have been nerfing threads going on I decided to start a new one
> and the topic is: Quest artifact wishing.
>
> Am I alone thinking that it is very peculiar that everybody but wizard
> can enjoy the Eye without level requirements and everybody but monk can
> do the same to the Eyes.
>
> The only quest artifact that doesn't work properly to others, than those
> who have earned it, is the PYEC.
>
> If wishing of quest artifacts is allowed shouldn't all of them be nerfed
> to cross-role adventurers? [1]

No.  In particular, the PYEC and Magic Mirror should have their odd
other-role restrictions removed, IMO.  It just doesn't make any sense,
and certainly doesn't make the game more fun, to have a handful of
them behave differently for other classes.  If you really want to nerf
them, outlaw quest artifact wishing (which, if you do it right, also
means bones-quashing them).  Personally I think the game's a bit more
interesting if you allow them, though.  But just making them behave
differently is a worst of both worlds compromise, IMO--especially
since it is _tough_ to do it meaningfully.

E.g. the PYEC is almost as useful to other classes as to tourists--you
really only _need_ blessed charging for /wishing, and the other _big_
charging target (markers) is unaffected by blessed/uncursed status in
the normal (use the charges up before recharging) case.  Other wands
you can just charge over and over, idem. rings, so blessed just
doesn't matter much.  It's nicer, but not hugely nicer.

OTOH, the Mirror's major interesting power is _gone_, completely.  For
other roles it's just MR/ESP rolled into one--items that just combine
a couple of other items' powers are extremely boring if occasionally
useful.  But basically the PYEC is made slightly less useful, while
the Mirror is stripped of all it's powers.

I'm opposed to changing quest artifacts' powers for off-role users,
but if you're going to do it at least nerf them approximately the same
amount.  I'd be tempted to strip the common powers (e.g. PYEC/Eye/
Mirror/etc lose magic resistance/ESP/telepathy but keep their special
power, rather than vice-versa) rather than the special ones (PW regen,
double spell damage).  Just stripping MR makes them a much bigger
gamble for early wishes--right now MR is a huge wish target, and you
can get it _and_ a very cool power "for free" with an early wish.  Get
rid of MR and the Eye still stays as one of the nicest items in the
game, but doesn't have the high impact on early survivability that MR
does--yet you still keep the diverse, interesting powers in the game.



